# graphify — the knowledge graph of this repo (see study/README.md).
# Same rule the corpus uses: BULK OUT, RECORD IN. What the lab PC needs to
# query the graph is committed, because D29 says handoff goes through git;
# what it can rebuild in one command, or what is machine-specific, is not.
#
#   committed   graph.json          1.0M  the graph itself. Rebuilding costs
#                                         ~334k LLM tokens across 3 agents.
#               GRAPH_REPORT.md      32K  god nodes, communities, audit trail
#               manifest.json        16K  lets `--update` re-extract only what
#                                         changed; contains no absolute paths
#               .graphify_labels.json 4K  the 68 community names, hand-written
#
#   ignored     graph.html          920K  one command from graph.json
#               cache/              1.2M  regenerable, and re-derived per machine
#               .graphify_python           an ABSOLUTE path to a Mac uv venv —
#               .graphify_root             committing these would break the lab PC
#               cost.json                  local token accounting
graphify-out/graph.html
graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/.graphify_python
graphify-out/.graphify_root
graphify-out/cost.json

# Phase 6 Step 4: the assembled Hugging Face Space bundle (space/build.py). A deployment, not source.
space/dist/

# Third-party skill packs installed with `npx skills add` (2026-09-20:
# Leonxlnx/taste-skill, 13 design/frontend skills, MIT). Pure Markdown, no
# executables — but they are vendored third-party instructions, and twelve of
# the thirteen are for landing pages, brand kits and image generation, which
# this repo does not have. `D105`'s precedent is the rule: a skill gets
# COMMITTED, with a `SOURCE.md` recording where it came from, WHEN IT IS USED
# for something measured here — that is how `webapp-testing` earned its place.
# Until one of these is used, it stays local.
.agents/
.claude/skills/brandkit
.claude/skills/design-taste-frontend
.claude/skills/design-taste-frontend-v1
.claude/skills/full-output-enforcement
.claude/skills/gpt-taste
.claude/skills/high-end-visual-design
.claude/skills/image-to-code
.claude/skills/imagegen-frontend-mobile
.claude/skills/imagegen-frontend-web
.claude/skills/industrial-brutalist-ui
.claude/skills/minimalist-ui
.claude/skills/redesign-existing-projects
.claude/skills/stitch-design-taste
